{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When your brother becomes poor etc.</b> Because he did commerce with the fruits of the Sabbatical year, as Rashi explained. And so we find in the days of Jeremiah that Israel were sold to idolaters because they profaned the Sabbatical year, as it is said: ויגל את השארית etc., and it is written: עד רצתה הארץ את שבתותיה." "<b>And his redeemer comes.</b> This is the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said: אשר לו אלהים קרובים אליו." "<b>And he redeems his brother's sale.</b> Jeremiah said to the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the Universe, You fulfilled for them 'when your brother becomes poor and sells of his possession'; fulfill for them 'and he redeems his brother's sale' — for You called them brothers, as it is said: למען אחי ורעי אדברה נא שלום בך, and thus it is written: למענכם שלחתי בבלה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:31.558522859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}